-## 6. Request Validation
+## 6. Rate Limiting Configuration
+
+The gateway reads rate limiting settings from `config/gateway.conf` at startup.
+Version-specific keys use `rate_limit_<version> = <requests>:<window_seconds>` and override the default global settings for matching request paths.
+
+```conf
+rate_limit_enabled = true
+rate_limit_requests = 100
+rate_limit_window_seconds = 60
+rate_limit_v1 = 60:60
+rate_limit_v2 = 500:60
+```
+
+| Key | Values | Description |
+|-----|--------|-------------|
+| `rate_limit_enabled` | `true` or `false` | Enables or disables per-client rate limiting. |
+| `rate_limit_requests` | Positive integer | Deprecated global/default maximum requests per client when no version-specific key matches. |
+| `rate_limit_window_seconds` | Positive integer | Deprecated global/default window length when no version-specific key matches. |
+| `rate_limit_<version>` | `<requests>:<seconds>` | Version-specific limit for routes such as `/v1/...` or `/v2/...`. |
+
+When a client exceeds the configured request count within the configured window,
+the gateway returns **429 Too Many Requests** with:
+
+```json
+{ "error": "Rate limit exceeded" }
+```
+
+---
